{#-
  Per-model Codex invoke + adapt + skip-relay recipe (PLAN-second-opinion-multi-model).

  This partial renders the recipe for ONE model (codex). It is included by
  `second_opinion_dispatch.md.j2` inside a per-model loop — the dispatch partial owns
  the `config.second_opinion.models` gating, so this file does NOT self-gate. Callers
  set `second_opinion_stage` ("review" | "plan") and `is_codex` (Codex-runtime flag)
  before the include.

  ADR-002/003 of PLAN-codex-second-opinion-sandbox (unchanged): the ORCHESTRATING MAIN
  LOOP (the stage prompt), NOT a tool-restricted reviewer subagent, runs Codex. Two layers
  escape Claude Code's Bash sandbox: (1) a settings.json `allow` rule (`Bash(codex exec:*)`)
  pre-approves the permission prompt, and (2) the orchestrator runs that ONE Bash call with
  the Bash tool parameter `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Codex stays hermetic via its own
  `--sandbox read-only --ignore-user-config --ignore-rules` flags.
-#}
{%- set _codex = (config.get('second_opinion', {}).get('codex', {})) if config else {} -%}
{%- set _stage = second_opinion_stage | default('review', true) %}
{%- set _is_codex = is_codex if is_codex is defined else false %}
**Invoke (codex).** Run Codex as a separate, sandbox-isolated step. Do NOT build the
prompt inside the same shell line as the `codex exec` call.

First create the temp files (ordinary sandboxed Bash) and note the two paths:

```bash
prompt_tmp=$(mktemp); out_tmp=$(mktemp); printf 'prompt=%s\nout=%s\n' "$prompt_tmp" "$out_tmp"
```

Then write the diff + {{ _stage }} context to the prompt-file path **using the
Write tool** — not a shell variable. The Write tool stores the bytes verbatim, so
command substitutions or backticks in adversarial diff text are never shell-expanded.
{% if not _is_codex %}
> **Sandbox escape (ADR-003, Claude Code only).** The `codex exec` call needs
> outbound network, which Claude Code's Bash sandbox blocks. Run THIS ONE Bash call
> with the Bash tool parameter **`dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`** — the
> `Bash(codex exec:*)` settings `allow` rule pre-approves the prompt, and Codex stays
> contained by its own `--sandbox read-only` flags. Do NOT disable the sandbox for
> any other command.
{%- else %}
> **Codex runtime note.** The Claude-Code Bash-tool sandbox-escape parameter and the
> `.claude/settings.json` allow rule do NOT apply on the Codex runtime — run the
> `codex exec` call directly and approve it per your Codex sandbox/approval policy.
> Codex stays contained by its own `--sandbox read-only` flags either way.
{%- endif %}
Finally run `codex exec` as its **own** Bash call — the command MUST begin with
`codex exec` so the `Bash(codex exec:*)` allow rule matches it:

```bash
codex exec --sandbox read-only {% if _codex.get('hermetic', true) %}--ignore-user-config --ignore-rules {% endif %}--output-schema {{ _codex.get('output_schema_path', '.claude/schemas/second-opinion-finding.schema.json') }} --output-last-message "$out_tmp" - < "$prompt_tmp"; echo "exit=$?"
```

**Adapt (status-guarded).** Only when the `codex exec` exit was 0, pipe the
output file through the adapter (deterministic — it maps severity
`critical→P0 / high→P1 / medium→P2 / low,info→P3`, sets `source: "codex"`, and sets
`needs_relaxation: true` when `file`/`line` is null; reading from the file keeps
untrusted Codex content out of the shell). Always clean up the temp files:

```bash
if [ "$exit" -eq 0 ]; then uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} python -m harness_maker.codex_adapter adapt --model codex < "$out_tmp"; fi; rm -f "$prompt_tmp" "$out_tmp"
```

**Skip relay (graceful degrade — ANY non-zero exit).** A non-zero `codex exec` exit means
the second opinion could not complete — the CLI is missing/removed (exit 127), `codex login`
expired, a rate-limit / subscription cap was hit, or the call errored. In every such case set
`status: "skipped"` for `model: "codex"` + a one-line reason, surface it (do NOT block —
warn-and-proceed), and append a best-effort ledger row. Pass each value as a **separate
`--flag`** (never inline an untrusted cause into a shell-quoted JSON blob — REVIEW security P1):

```bash
reason="<one-line cause>"; uv run --with {{ harness_maker_src_path }} python -m harness_maker.codex_ledger emit --slug "<slug>" --stage {{ _stage }} --model codex --finding-ref "n/a" --disposition unresolved --status skipped --skip-reason "$reason"
```

On success set `status: "invoked"` for codex. A silently-degraded second opinion is the H4
failure mode — the `/hm:health` smoke check is the positive backstop.
